#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:5
#: 1fbafe2f4ee04524960c9275c7936d67
msgid "Tuning the Balance Bot"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:8
#: 5e37ea61ded147779e9d9f24879dc305
msgid "Tuning Pitch Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:10
#: e922fb342afd418981c9c7b2a91e031a
msgid "The Pitch controller should be tuned in Manual mode. The parameters involved in tuning this controller are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:12
#: 0e3ec62fa1d2453c9216a2209bde6b3e
msgid ":ref:`BAL_PITCH_MAX<BAL_PITCH_MAX>`: Pitch angle limit.  If the user provides full throttle the vehicle will attempt to lean at this angle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:13
#: f0f5d99c1baa409881ab28f536a411da
msgid ":ref:`BAL_PITCH_TRIM <BAL_PITCH_TRIM>`: Pitch trim to offset tilt of center of mass"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:14
#: f6014ae055f84a8bb855c6a53a1211ec
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_PIT_FF <ATC_BAL_PIT_FF>`: Feed forward gain using the current pitch angle.  This should normally be set to 0.4"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:15
#: 76666ec0eb63426384c0c5a13c62285f
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_FF <ATC_BAL_FF>`: Feed forward gain using desired pitch angle.  This should normally be set to 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:16
#: 391f286b7b584b19b02254837c338f1f
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_P <ATC_BAL_P>`: P gain used to correct the current pitch angle error.  Higher values will result in faster error correction but if too high will lead to oscillation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:17
#: d301c05f8baf4136949bb05ccfe5c34d
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_I <ATC_BAL_I>`: I gain used to correct long term pitch angle errors.  Setting to the same value as P often works well.  If set too high this could lead to slow oscillations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:18
#: fd059f960a7d4395ab0ea2128bf3e1ed
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_D <ATC_BAL_D>`: D gain used to correct changes in pitch angle error.  Setting to higher values may result in a more stable pitch control but if too high can lead to very fast oscillations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:19
#: c4fd879af2804718b263ae996d7196d3
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_IMAX <ATC_BAL_IMAX>`: I term maximum value.  This should normally be set to 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:20
#: 9d4d22963390400a8ec30f585576b787
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_FLTT <ATC_BAL_FLTT>`: Filter applied to the desired pitch angle.  Lower values lead to a slower moving desired pitch angle target.  Higher values lead to a more responsive pitch target"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:21
#: a87b7115fcf54d8d996e8be84f195a41
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_FLTE <ATC_BAL_FLTE>`: Filter applied to the pitch error.  Lower values lead to a slower response to pitch angle errors.  Higher values lead to a faster response"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:22
#: dcbae24560e144bdbc986a2ba34a81d2
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_FLTD <ATC_BAL_FLTD>`: Filter applied to the pitch error applied to the D term.  Lower values lead to a slower response to changes in pitch angle errors.  Higher values lead to a faster response"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:24
#: 8dfb1f94fef141b1bfa5340f7dd85124
msgid "Good tuning of the pitch controller is crucial for tuning other Control Modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:27
#: 807fa57f84cb465cb853c8c285decf96
msgid "Real-time Tuning of Pitch Control"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:29
#: f5019012fd2f4fe6be7b55327614ef99
msgid "It is best to connect the ground station (e.g. Mission Planner) to the vehicle using a telemetry radio and then enable real-time display of the Pitch PID controller's inputs and outputs by doing the following"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:31
#: 8dea08e5ae6a49b38af85cfa2a16d4c0
msgid "Set :ref:`GCS_PID_MASK <GCS_PID_MASK>` = 4 (Pitch)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:32
#: da3990a7c62347b6b26a411498e97bb9
msgid "Connect with Mission Planner, go to the Data screen and check the \"Tuning\" checkbox in the bottom middle.  From the large \"Display This\" window check \"piddesired\", \"pidachieved\" and optionally \"pidP\", \"pidI\" and \"pidD\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:33
#: c2411e5f7c734d10b94f96332c5db521
msgid "Speed up the rate of the PID_TUNING messages using Mission Planner's Ctrl-F Message Interval feature"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:38
#: 8aee2e8a9ed7479cbcde3c8317046bdd
msgid "Stand the vehicle upright and arm in Manual mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:39
#: 9b5490ea639b44aa97ea5a728e952a45
msgid "With the throttle stick in the middle the \"piddesired\" should always be zero while the \"pidachieved\" will move as the vehicle pitches back and forth"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:40
#: fa70f9b6b36440d4baf48d419687c33c
msgid "Open Mission Planner's Config Full Parameter Tree and adjust :ref:`ATC_BAL_P <ATC_BAL_P>`, :ref:`ATC_BAL_I <ATC_BAL_I>` and :ref:`ATC_BAL_D <ATC_BAL_D>` gains so that \"pidachieved\" follows \"piddesired\" (e.g. stays near zero)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:41
#: b4536fc9fdb848b1a451ea0b34237ec0
msgid "The vehicle may drift off in either direction so be ready to catch it and return it to its original position.  Drifting is not necessarily a problem at this stage, the goal is for \"pidachieved\" to follow \"piddesired\" as closely as possible"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:42
#: e8025dc836364e81ad83e8bdf8c06501
msgid "Apply throttle stick inputs which should result in \"piddesired\" changing.  Continue to adjust the gains so \"pidachieved\" tracks well"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:44
#: 03cfab3bf12e44f38b2c0a5e2a4260a0
msgid "A good tuning methodology is to increase P and I in turn: Increase P until the vehicle starts to oscillate, then increase I until the vehicle starts to wobble back and forth. Once this gives a reasonably good response, D can be increased to increase responsiveness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:47
#: 78241d85fb0945b69ef4a5cacfee7845
msgid "Stable PID values for ATC_BAL_* can be quite large, particularly for small vehicles. Good starting values are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:49
#: 6b5ea595258243008b510947403cc1fd
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_P <ATC_BAL_P>` = 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:50
#: cb73abfd2feb4505a2c1ec7cd46b89e1
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_I <ATC_BAL_I>` = 8"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:51
#: e9c320f2e13d4933b16bc832b7c85456
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_D <ATC_BAL_D>` = 0.1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:54
#: 98041a13c2704799ad25255a9a3d5649
msgid "Motor Dead Zone and Expo"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:56
#: 9fbe2acfae2f44a6b1b8feeb2445cbd7
msgid ":ref:`MOT_THST_EXPO <MOT_THST_EXPO>` is recommended to be -0.5, to give a stable pitch angle at both small and large pitch angles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:61
#: 7613dcc031c54a3bb34206272205906f
msgid "Reducing Drift with Pitch Trim"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:63
#: 4aab5d5244a64858a7dc9099f030d829
msgid "If the vehicle consistently drifts in one direction while upright in Manual mode the center of mass may be slightly off of center.  :ref:`BAL_PITCH_TRIM <BAL_PITCH_TRIM>` sets the default pitch angle at zero throttle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:65
#: c2fbc473d1e5464fa4037f47308c33a8
msgid "If the balance bot drifts forward, increase :ref:`BAL_PITCH_TRIM <BAL_PITCH_TRIM>` in steps of 0.1 until the vehicle's drift is reduced.  If the balance bot drifts backwards, decrease :ref:`BAL_PITCH_TRIM <BAL_PITCH_TRIM>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:68
#: 06b8f0a51026439bbb949a5100490260
msgid "Pitch Limiting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:70
#: 5e21b142b4d04981859bc6967b2cb39c
msgid "Rover-4.3 (and higher) includes automatic pitch limiting to reduce the chance of the vehicle falling over due to throttle saturation.  The feature works by monitoring the throttle output and if it crosses a given threshold the maximum pitch angle is temporarily reduced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:72
#: 6ccb4dd1000345c58da769dd17c596da
msgid "The parameters below can be used to tune this features although normally they can be left at their default values"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:74
#: 4ba6c8a43d93434696eb8146807dbfc8
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_LIM_THR<ATC_BAL_LIM_THR>`: pitch limit feature's throttle threshold (expressed as a value between 0 and 1).  If the vehicle's throttle climbs above this limit the vehicle's maximum pitch angle will be reduced."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:75
#: f0758fd697f140fca02a523943022e92
msgid ":ref:`ATC_BAL_LIM_TC<ATC_BAL_LIM_TC>`: pitch limit feature's time constant.  Lower values will cause the pitch limit to be reduced quickly.  Higher values will limit the pitch more slowly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:83
#: b03fcb64af28467c9b7061c0e97e55d0
msgid "Tuning Acro Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:85
#: 1a49c8017e81460d8c4321aff85d619e
msgid "The following parameters should be set"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:87
#: 54319ddd571f48539ffbe4ab7fb008bb
msgid ":ref:`CRUISE_THROTTLE <CRUISE_THROTTLE>` = 0 (This parameter can cause conflicts otherwise, in Balance Bots)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:88
#: c0436c251d7c4407be433c05a70eb87e
msgid ":ref:`CRUISE_SPEED <CRUISE_SPEED>`: Maximum speed limit for Speed Controller. To be set by trial and error"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:90
#: 5334740d2a3644cd8110eaae44d49a73
msgid "With the above parameters set, follow the tuning guides for :ref:`Speed <rover-tuning-throttle-and-speed>` and :ref:`Steering<rover-tuning-steering-rate>`. Another important thing to note is that the feed-forward term described in these pages does not make any positive contribution in a balance bot and is best, set to zero."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:93
#: f8335eedede54f9a887b1160df22bba5
msgid "Guided, Auto, RTL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:95
#: 675303c880c44e4ba693918281907fba
msgid "Follow the :ref:`Navigation tuning instructions <rover-tuning-navigation>` to tune the vehicle for autonomous modes including Guided, Auto and RTL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:97
#: 9a5fb208060e4a129fa16527661ed9b9
msgid "Optionally it may be convenient to automatically change the mode to Acro after an Auto mission is completed by setting"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/balance_bot-tuning.rst:99
#: f86227764e85445e9ba88d4df127891c
msgid ":ref:`MIS_DONE_BEHAVE <MIS_DONE_BEHAVE>` = 2 (Acro)"
msgstr ""
